.TH L10N-CONV 1 "February 2026" "l10n-conv 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
l10n-conv \- universal localization file converter, validator, and compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B l10n-conv
[\fIGLOBAL_OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND_OPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B l10n-conv
is a comprehensive tool for working with localization files across
multiple formats. It provides conversion between 16+ localization formats,
validation of translation files, compilation of source formats to binary
formats, extraction of translatable strings from source code, and various
other localization workflow operations.

Supported formats include GNU gettext PO/MO, Qt Linguist TS/QM, XLIFF 1.2/2.0/2.1,
Android XML, iOS/macOS Strings, JSON (various schemas), YAML, Java Properties,
Microsoft RESX, Mozilla Fluent, PHP arrays, TBX (TermBase eXchange), and more.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-about
Show comprehensive application information including version, supported
formats, feature overview, and copyright details. This provides a complete
reference for supported functionality.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output mode. Shows detailed processing information including
file analysis, conversion steps, validation results, and timing data.
Useful for debugging and understanding tool behavior.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Format all output as JSON for programmatic consumption. This affects
all commands that produce structured output including stats, check,
diff, and list-formats. Error messages remain in plain text.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-essential output. Only display errors and final results.
Progress indicators, informational messages, and warnings are hidden.
Exit codes still indicate success/failure status.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Display version information including build date and supported
format versions, then exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B convert \fIINPUT\fR [\-f \fIFORMAT\fR] [\-\-to \fIFORMAT\fR] [\-o \fIOUTPUT\fR] [\-\-dry-run] [\-\-batch]
Convert localization files between different formats. The tool automatically
detects the input format unless explicitly specified with \-f. Output format
is determined by \-\-to or inferred from the output filename extension.

.RS 8
.TP
.BR \-f " " \fIFORMAT\fR ", " \-\-from " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Explicitly specify input format (overrides auto-detection)
.TP
.BR \-\-to " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Specify output format (required if not inferrable from output filename)
.TP
.BR \-o " " \fIOUTPUT\fR ", " \-\-output " " \fIOUTPUT\fR
Output file path (required for most conversions)
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Preview the conversion without writing output files
.TP
.BR \-\-batch
Process multiple files recursively in directories
.RE
.TP
.B compile \fIINPUT\fR \-o \fIOUTPUT\fR [\-\-dry-run]
Compile localization source files to binary formats. Supports PO→MO
(GNU gettext) and TS→QM (Qt Linguist) compilation. The output format
is automatically determined from the input format.

.RS 8
.TP
.BR \-o " " \fIOUTPUT\fR ", " \-\-output " " \fIOUTPUT\fR
Output file path (required)
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be compiled without creating files
.RE
.TP
.B extract \fISOURCE_DIR\fR \-o \fIOUTPUT\fR [\-f \fIFORMAT\fR] [\-\-dry-run]
Extract translatable strings from source code files. Supports Python
(gettext calls), C/C++ (printf-style, gettext), JavaScript/TypeScript
(i18n functions), and QML (qsTr functions). Creates template files
suitable for translation.

.RS 8
.TP
.BR \-o " " \fIOUTPUT\fR ", " \-\-output " " \fIOUTPUT\fR
Output template file path (required)
.TP
.BR \-f " " \fIFORMAT\fR ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format for extracted strings (default: po)
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Show what strings would be extracted without creating files
.RE
.TP
.B check \fIFILE\fR [\-f \fIFORMAT\fR]
Validate a localization file for syntax errors, missing translations,
format consistency, and other common issues. Reports problems with
specific line numbers and suggested fixes where applicable.

.RS 8
.TP
.BR \-f " " \fIFORMAT\fR ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Explicitly specify file format (overrides auto-detection)
.RE
.TP
.B stats \fIFILE\fR [\-f \fIFORMAT\fR]
Display comprehensive translation statistics including total strings,
translated count, fuzzy entries, untranslated entries, completion
percentage, and file-specific metadata.

.RS 8
.TP
.BR \-f " " \fIFORMAT\fR ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Explicitly specify file format (overrides auto-detection)
.RE
.TP
.B merge \fIBASE\fR \fIUPDATE\fR \-o \fIOUTPUT\fR [\-f \fIFORMAT\fR] [\-\-dry-run]
Merge two localization files, combining translations from an update
file into a base file. Handles conflicts by preserving newer translations
and maintaining existing metadata where possible.

.RS 8
.TP
.BR \-o " " \fIOUTPUT\fR ", " \-\-output " " \fIOUTPUT\fR
Output merged file path (required)
.TP
.BR \-f " " \fIFORMAT\fR ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Specify format for all files (default: auto-detect)
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Preview merge results without creating output file
.RE
.TP
.B diff \fIFILE1\fR \fIFILE2\fR [\-f \fIFORMAT\fR]
Compare two localization files and show differences in translations,
added/removed entries, and metadata changes. Useful for reviewing
translation updates and changes between versions.

.RS 8
.TP
.BR \-f " " \fIFORMAT\fR ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Specify format for both files (default: auto-detect)
.RE
.TP
.B init \fITEMPLATE\fR \-l \fILANG\fR \-o \fIOUTPUT\fR [\-f \fIFORMAT\fR] [\-\-dry-run]
Create a new language-specific translation file from a template.
Initializes proper locale metadata and prepares the file structure
for translation work.

.RS 8
.TP
.BR \-l " " \fILANG\fR ", " \-\-language " " \fILANG\fR
Target language code (e.g., 'de', 'fr-CA', 'pt-BR') (required)
.TP
.BR \-o " " \fIOUTPUT\fR ", " \-\-output " " \fIOUTPUT\fR
Output file path (required)
.TP
.BR \-f " " \fIFORMAT\fR ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format (default: same as template)
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Preview initialization without creating files
.RE
.TP
.B list-formats
Display all supported input and output formats with detailed descriptions,
file extensions, and feature support matrix. This command provides
a comprehensive reference for format capabilities.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Operation completed successfully without errors.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error occurred (file not found, invalid format, write error, etc.).
.TP
.B 2
Warnings were encountered but operation completed. Issues were found
during validation or conversion that should be reviewed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Convert PO file to XLIFF format:
.B l10n-conv convert messages.po \-\-to xliff \-o messages.xliff
.TP
Batch convert all PO files to JSON:
.B l10n-conv convert po/ \-\-to json \-o json/ \-\-batch
.TP
Compile PO to binary MO format:
.B l10n-conv compile messages.po \-o messages.mo
.TP
Extract strings from Python source code:
.B l10n-conv extract src/ \-o messages.pot
.TP
Extract to TS format for Qt projects:
.B l10n-conv extract qml_src/ \-o translations.ts \-f ts
.TP
Validate XLIFF file for issues:
.B l10n-conv check translations.xliff
.TP
Show detailed statistics in JSON format:
.B l10n-conv stats messages.po \-\-json
.TP
Merge updated translations into base file:
.B l10n-conv merge base.po updates.po \-o merged.po
.TP
Compare two translation files:
.B l10n-conv diff old.po new.po
.TP
Initialize German translation from template:
.B l10n-conv init template.pot \-l de \-o de.po
.TP
Preview conversion without writing files:
.B l10n-conv convert input.ts \-\-to po \-o output.po \-\-dry\-run
.TP
List all supported formats:
.B l10n-conv list\-formats
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
.B l10n-conv
supports the following localization formats:
.RS 4
.B GNU gettext:
PO (Portable Object), MO (Machine Object), POT (Template)
.br
.B Qt Linguist:
TS (Translation Source), QM (Qt Message)
.br
.B XLIFF:
XLIFF 1.2, XLIFF 2.0, XLIFF 2.1
.br
.B Mobile:
Android XML, iOS/macOS Strings, iOS Stringsdict
.br
.B Web:
JSON (i18next, FormatJS, Chrome i18n), YAML (Rails i18n)
.br
.B Enterprise:
Java Properties, Microsoft RESX, TBX (TermBase eXchange)
.br
.B Modern:
Mozilla Fluent (FTL), Gettext JavaScript (JED)
.br
.B Legacy:
PHP arrays, Windows RC, CSV
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/l10n-conv/
User configuration directory
.TP
.B ~/.config/l10n-conv/formats.json
Custom format definitions
.TP
.B ~/.config/l10n-conv/extractors.json
Custom string extraction rules
